      "text": "To find the ratio of \\( AC \\) to \\( BD \\), we start by determining the lengths of the segments \\( AC \\) and \\( BD \\) using the given distances \\( AB \\), \\( BC \\), and \\( AD \\).\n\nFirst, we know:\n\\[ AB = 2 \\text{ units} \\]\n\\[ BC = 5 \\text{ units} \\]\n\\[ AD = 14 \\text{ units} \\]\n\nSince points \\( A \\), \\( B \\), \\( C \\), and \\( D \\) lie on a line in that order, the length of \\( AC \\) is the sum of \\( AB \\) and \\( BC \\):\n\\[ AC = AB + BC = 2 + 5 = 7 \\text{ units} \\]\n\nThe length of \\( BD \\) is the difference between \\( AD \\) and \\( AB \\):\n\\[ BD = AD - AB = 14 - 2 = 12 \\text{ units} \\]\n\nNow, we need to find the ratio of \\( AC \\) to \\( BD \\):\n\\[ \\text{Ratio of } AC \\text{ to } BD = \\frac{AC}{BD} = \\frac{7}{12} \\]\n\nThus, the ratio of \\( AC \\) to \\( BD \\) is:\n\\[ \\boxed{\\frac{7}{12}} \\]",
