      "text": "To solve for the ratio of \\( AC \\) to \\( BD \\), we first need to determine the lengths of \\( AC \\) and \\( BD \\) on the given line.\n\nGiven:\n- \\( AB = 2 \\) units\n- \\( BC = 5 \\) units\n- \\( AD = 14 \\) units\n\nWe start by finding the lengths of \\( AC \\) and \\( BD \\).\n\nSince points \\( A \\), \\( B \\), \\( C \\), and \\( D \\) lie on a line in that order, the total length of \\( AD \\) can be expressed as the sum of the lengths of \\( AB \\), \\( BC \\), and \\( CD \\):\n\\[ AD = AB + BC + CD \\]\nSubstituting the given values:\n\\[ 14 = 2 + 5 + CD \\]\nSolving for \\( CD \\):\n\\[ 14 = 7 + CD \\]\n\\[ CD = 14 - 7 \\]\n\\[ CD = 7 \\]\n\nNow, we calculate the length of \\( AC \\):\n\\[ AC = AB + BC \\]\n\\[ AC = 2 + 5 \\]\n\\[ AC = 7 \\]\n\nNext, we calculate the length of \\( BD \\):\n\\[ BD = BC + CD \\]\n\\[ BD = 5 + 7 \\]\n\\[ BD = 12 \\]\n\nWe need to find the ratio of \\( AC \\) to \\( BD \\):\n\\[ \\text{Ratio of } AC \\text{ to } BD = \\frac{AC}{BD} = \\frac{7}{12} \\]\n\nThus, the ratio of \\( AC \\) to \\( BD \\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{7}{12}}\n\\]\n\nXena is trying to outrun a dragon to get to the safety of a cave it's too big to fit into. Xena has a 600 foot head start, but the dragon can burn her if it gets within 120 feet of her. If Xena runs 15 feet per second and the dragon flies 30 feet per second, how many seconds does Xena have to get to the cave?\nTo determine how long Xena has to get to the cave, we need to calculate the time it takes for the dragon to close the distance from its current position to Xena's starting position. Initially, Xena has a 600-foot head start, and the dragon can burn Xena if it gets within 120 feet of her. Therefore, the dragon must not get within 120 feet of Xena's starting position within the time it takes for Xena to cover the remaining distance.\n\nFirst, let's calculate the maximum distance the dragon can cover in the time it takes Xena to run \\(d\\) feet:\n\\[ \\text{Time for Xena to run } d \\text{ feet} = \\frac{d}{15} \\text{ seconds} \\]\nDuring this time, the dragon covers:\n\\[ \\text{Distance covered by the dragon} = 30 \\times \\frac{d}{15} = 2d \\text{ feet} \\]\nSo, the distance the dragon needs to cover to reach within 120 feet of Xena is:\n\\[ 600 - 120 = 480 \\text{ feet} \\]\nThus, we need to find \\(d\\) such that:\n\\[ 2d \\geq 480 \\]\nSolving for \\(d\\):\n\\[ d \\geq \\frac{480}{2} = 240 \\text{ feet} \\]\nTherefore, Xena has to cover at least 240 feet to be sure the dragon doesn't burn her. The time it takes for Xena to cover 240 feet is:\n\\[ \\text{Time} = \\frac{240}{15} = 16 \\text{ seconds} \\]\nSince the dragon needs to cover at most 480 feet to get within 120 feet of Xena, the maximum time it takes for the dragon to reach within 120 feet of Xena is:\n\\[ \\text{Time for dragon to cover 480 feet} = \\frac{480}{30} = 16 \\text{ seconds} \\]\nSince Xena can cover 240 feet in 16 seconds and the dragon needs at least 16 seconds to reach within 120 feet of her, Xena has at least 16 seconds to get to the cave. Therefore, the time Xena has to get to the cave is:\n\\[ \\boxed{16} \\]\n\nThe mules Alberto on professionalizes.\nCorrected based on given context to ensure grammatically consistent structure was fulfilled.\n\nOn a well-monitored engagement, competent mules under Alberto's company undergo comprehensive professional development routines.\nThe above sentence is coherent and correctly punctuated. Let's break down the sentence for clarity:\n\n1. \"On a well-monitored engagement\" provides context for the specific professionalization.\n2. \"competent mules\" refers to the mules being professionally developed.\n3. \"under Alberto's company\" shows the origin or provider of the mules.\n4. \"undergo comprehensive professional development routines\" describes the process of professionalizing.\n\nThus, the corrected sentence is:\n\n\"On a well-monitored engagement, competent mules under Alberto's company undergo comprehensive professional development routines.\"\n\nThe correct usage was kept intact, ensuring clear understanding and grammatical consistency.",
