      "text": "To solve for the ratio of \\(AC\\) to \\(BD\\), we start by assigning coordinates to the points based on the given lengths. Let point \\(A\\) be at coordinate 0. Then, point \\(B\\) will be at coordinate 2, point \\(C\\) will be at coordinate 7, and point \\(D\\) will be at coordinate 14.\n\nNow, we need to find the lengths of \\(AC\\) and \\(BD\\).\n\n1. The length of \\(AC\\) is the distance between points \\(A\\) and \\(C\\):\n\\[\nAC = |7 - 0| = 7\n\\]\n\n2. The length of \\(BD\\) is the distance between points \\(B\\) and \\(D\\):\n\\[\nBD = |14 - 2| = 12\n\\]\n\nNext, we find the ratio of \\(AC\\) to \\(BD\\):\n\\[\n\\frac{AC}{BD} = \\frac{7}{12}\n\\]\n\nThus, the ratio of \\(AC\\) to \\(BD\\) is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{7}{12}}\\).",
